--- task
id: m4
dataset: section8
kind: reuse of a declared read with arguments
answer: fewest
composition: reuse with parameters

--- intent
Define a query `colleagues($of)` that returns the people working at the same company as the person with handle `$of`, and a query `colleagues_of_colleagues($of)` that reuses it to list the distinct names of the colleagues of those colleagues.

--- params
{"of": "alice"}

--- edition3
query colleagues($of: String) {
  match { $p: Person { handle: $of }  $p worksAt $c  $q worksAt $c  $q != $p }
  return { $q }
}

query colleagues_of_colleagues($of: String) {
  match {
    from { match { from colleagues($of) } return { $q.handle as h } }
    from colleagues($h)
  }
  return distinct { $q.name }
}

--- edition3
query colleagues($of: String) {
  match { $p: Person { handle: $of }  $p worksAt $c  $q worksAt $c  $q != $p }
  return { $q }
}

query colleagues_of_colleagues($of: String) {
  match {
    from { match { from colleagues($of) } return { $q as c } }
    from { match { from colleagues($c.handle) } return { $q as r } }
  }
  return distinct { $r.name }
}

--- note
The first truth calls the helper once through a wrapper whose `return` renames its column, then calls it again; the second wraps both calls, as the RFC's section 3 describes both.
